    <paragraph>Determine if a Relation is a Function</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use the set of ordered pairs to ⓐ determine whether the relation is a function, ⓑ find the domain of the relation, and ⓒ find the range of the relation.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="295" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ {\left( {-3,9} \right),\left( {-2,4} \right),\left( {-1,1} \right),} \right.$$ $$\left. {\left( {0,0} \right),}\left( {1,1} \right),\left( {2,4} \right),\left( {3,9} \right) \right\}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ yes ⓑ {−3, −2, −1, 0, 1, 2, 3} ⓒ {9, 4, 1, 0}</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="296" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ {\left( {9,-3} \right),\left( {4,-2} \right),\left( {1,-1} \right),} \right.$$ $$\left. {\left( {0,0} \right),}{\left( {1,1} \right),}\left( {4,2} \right),\left( {9,3} \right) \right\}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="297" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ {\left( {-3,27} \right),\left( {-2,8} \right),\left( {-1,1} \right),} \right.$$ $$\left. {\left( {0,0} \right),\left( {1,1} \right),}{\left( {2,8} \right),\left( {3,27} \right)} \right\}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ yes ⓑ {−3, −2, −1, 0, 1, 2, 3} ⓒ 0, 1, 8, 27}</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="298" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ {\left( {-3,-27} \right),\left( {-2,-8} \right),\left( {-1,-1} \right),} \right.$$ $$\left. {\left( {0,0} \right),\left( {1,1} \right),}\left( {2,8} \right),\left( {3,27} \right) \right\}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
