    <paragraph>In the following exercises, evaluate the function: ⓐ $$g(h^{2})$$ ⓑ $$g(x + 2)$$ ⓒ $$g(x) + g(2).$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="315" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$g(x) = 2x + 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$g(h2)=2h2+1g(h2)=2h2+1$$ ⓑ $$g(x+2)=2x+5g(x+2)=2x+5$$ ⓒ $$g(x)+g(2)=2x+6g(x)+g(2)=2x+6$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="316" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$g(x) = 5x - 8$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="317" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$g(x) = -3x - 2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$g(h2)=-3h2-2g(h2)=-3h2-2$$ ⓑ $$g(x+2)=-3x-8g(x+2)=-3x-8$$ ⓒ $$g(x)+g(2)=-3x-10g(x)+g(2)=-3x-10$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="318" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$g(x) = -8x + 2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="319" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$g(x) = 3 - x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$g(h2)=3-h2g(h2)=3-h2$$ ⓑ $$g(x+2)=1-xg(x+2)=1-x$$ ⓒ $$g(x)+g(2)=4-xg(x)+g(2)=4-x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="320" has_solution="false">
